1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:08,948
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Orthic Triangle H a H b H c and the Tangential Triangle T A T B T C form a classic dual pair.

2
00:00:08,948 --> 00:00:22,730
The orthic triangle is both the cevian and pedal triangle of the Orthocenter X four, while the tangential triangle is bounded by the tangents to the circumcircle at A, B, and C, with perspector at the Symmedian Point X six.

3
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:35,205
Because the circumcircle radius to each vertex A, B, C is perpendicular to the corresponding side of the orthic triangle, the sides of the orthic triangle and the sides of the tangential triangle are strictly parallel!

4
00:00:35,205 --> 00:00:38,800
Consequently, the orthic and tangential triangles are homothetic.

5
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:51,540
In acute triangles, the Orthocenter X four is the incenter of the orthic triangle, while the radical axis and cross-intersections of the orthic and reference triangles produce the Clawson Point X nineteen.
